            <div xml:id="d342">

                <pb facs="0284" n="272" xml:id="pg272"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A.R.–N.C./20: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-01-29T18:00:00-04:30">January 29, 1940—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. Department’s circular January 27, 3 p.m. The Foreign Minister informs me that
                    the position of the Venezuelan Government is identical with our own and
                    instructions to that effect have been sent Venezuela’s delegate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
